    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve $88 \\div 4 \\div 2$, we first observe that division is written horizontally, so we treat it as a series of steps to integrate:\n\n1. Calculate $88 \\div 4$:\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align*}\n   88 & \\div 4 = 22\n   \\end{align*}\n   \\]\n\n2. Now, we have $22 \\div 2$. Dividing by 2 can be converted into halving:\n\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align*}\n   22 & \\div 2 = \\frac{22}{2} = 11\n   \\end{align*}\n   \\]\n\nWhen we have no remainder (a term referring to the situation when a divisor is larger than the dividend at each step and continuous divisons occur) after dividing, no further division is needed. But in this example, since we only had one step division, we stop where division will become necessary. Hence, the result is simply the dividend divided by 2 at the last step.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is (B) $\\boxed{11}$.",
